From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:59:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(food): no push on the amounts, fat only on evidence,
 default effort
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On 60 weighed Nutrition5k plates the first version over-estimated energy by a further 36 kcal
(MAPE 63.7 % against 53.2 % for the old prompt): told that large portions are the ones
underestimated and to assume cooking fat, the model inflated every plate, while its
composition per gram was right. The prompt now sizes the food against the references without a
direction, lists cooking fat, dressing or sauce only on a visual cue or the wearer's note, and
sends no effort setting (high cost 2.2× the tokens and sized nothing better). Grams ×
composition per 100 g, the "what the photo cannot show" note and the hint stay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/main/java/com/noop/food/FoodVision.kt | 39 ++++++++-----------
 .../com/noop/food/FoodVisionRequestTest.kt    | 11 +++---
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/app/src/main/java/com/noop/food/FoodVision.kt b/android/app/src/main/java/com/noop/food/FoodVision.kt
index 65a66f55e..b4e8dd0a3 100644
--- a/android/app/src/main/java/com/noop/food/FoodVision.kt
+++ b/android/app/src/main/java/com/noop/food/FoodVision.kt
@@ -64,12 +64,6 @@ object FoodVision {
     private const val API_VERSION = "2023-06-01"
     private val JSON = "application/json; charset=utf-8".toMediaType()
 
-    /**
-     * Thinking depth for a photo. Opus 5.5 defaults to `medium`; sizing the portions is the part the
-     * published evaluations find hardest, so the request asks for `high`.
-     */
-    internal const val EFFORT = "high"
-
     /** One item of the reply, in the order the model writes them: what it is, how much, then what it is made of. */
     internal val ITEM_FIELDS = listOf("name", "portion", "grams", "kcal_per_100g", "protein_per_100g", "carbs_per_100g", "fat_per_100g")
 
@@ -186,10 +180,12 @@ object FoodVision {
 
     /**
      * The instructions, one step per lever the 2024-2026 evaluations found to cut the error: name every
-     * food including the hidden layers, size each one against known objects instead of a typical
-     * serving (large portions are the ones underestimated), add the cooking fat and sauces that do not
-     * show as items of their own, and give grams plus composition per 100 g rather than a kcal guess.
-     * The notes end with the one thing the photo cannot show, so the wearer can correct it.
+     * food including the hidden layers, size each one against known objects, list the cooking fat and
+     * sauces the photo or the note gives evidence of as items of their own, and give grams plus
+     * composition per 100 g rather than a kcal guess. The notes end with the one thing the photo cannot
+     * show, so the wearer can correct it. No push in either direction: told that large portions are
+     * underestimated and to assume cooking fat, the model over-estimated 60 weighed plates by a further
+     * 36 kcal (Nutrition5k, 2026-10-20).
      */
     internal fun prompt(note: String, structured: Boolean, photos: Int = 1): String = buildString {
         if (photos > 1) {
@@ -203,14 +199,12 @@ object FoodVision {
         append("1. Foods: list each distinct food or drink as one item, including what is partly hidden (the rice ")
         append("under a stew, the filling of a sandwich, the sauce under the meat). The meal is from Spain unless ")
         append("the note says otherwise.\n")
-        append("2. Amounts: judge each amount from the scene, never from a typical serving. Size references: a dinner ")
-        append("plate is about 26 cm across, a dessert plate 20 cm, a fork or spoon 19 cm, a glass 250 ml, a hand ")
-        append("18 cm. Estimate the area each food covers and how high it is piled, then its weight in grams ")
-        append("(ml for drinks). Large or heaped portions are the ones most often underestimated.\n")
-        append("3. Hidden fat: decide how each food was cooked and list the cooking fat, dressing or sauce that does ")
-        append("not show as its own item (olive oil is the default fat in Spain): about 10 g of oil for a sautéed ")
-        append("or grilled portion, 15-20 g for fried or breaded food, 10-15 g for a dressed salad, unless the ")
-        append("note says otherwise.\n")
+        append("2. Amounts: judge each amount from the scene. Size references: a dinner plate is about 26 cm across, ")
+        append("a dessert plate 20 cm, a fork or spoon 19 cm, a glass 250 ml, a hand 18 cm. Estimate the area each ")
+        append("food covers and how high it is piled, then its weight in grams (ml for drinks).\n")
+        append("3. Hidden fat: decide how each food was cooked. When there is a visual cue (a sheen of oil, a fried ")
+        append("or breaded coating, a visible dressing or sauce) or the note says so, list the cooking fat, dressing ")
+        append("or sauce as its own item (olive oil is the default fat in Spain); do not add fat on assumption alone.\n")
         append("4. Composition: for each item give grams and the kcal, protein, carbs and fat PER 100 g from ")
         append("standard food composition tables (BEDCA, USDA). The totals are computed from grams × per 100 g, ")
         append("so never bend the per-100 g values to fit a guessed total.\n")
@@ -238,8 +232,9 @@ object FoodVision {
 
     /**
      * The Messages API body: model, reply cap, one user turn of [image…, text], and (when
-     * [structured]) `output_config` with [outputSchema] as the format and [EFFORT]. Never
-     * temperature/top_p/thinking/tool_choice: Claude 5.x answers those with HTTP 400.
+     * [structured]) `output_config.format` with [outputSchema]. Never temperature/top_p/thinking/
+     * tool_choice: Claude 5.x answers those with HTTP 400. No `effort` either: `high` cost 2.2× the
+     * tokens of the default and sized the portions no better.
      */
     internal fun buildRequestBody(model: String, imagesBase64: List<String>, note: String, structured: Boolean): JSONObject {
         val content = JSONArray()
@@ -267,9 +262,7 @@ object FoodVision {
         if (structured) {
             body.put(
                 "output_config",
-                JSONObject()
-                    .put("format", JSONObject().put("type", "json_schema").put("schema", outputSchema()))
-                    .put("effort", EFFORT),
+                JSONObject().put("format", JSONObject().put("type", "json_schema").put("schema", outputSchema())),
             )
         }
         return body
diff --git a/android/app/src/test/java/com/noop/food/FoodVisionRequestTest.kt b/android/app/src/test/java/com/noop/food/FoodVisionRequestTest.kt
index 9d1670614..732a65bf4 100644
--- a/android/app/src/test/java/com/noop/food/FoodVisionRequestTest.kt
+++ b/android/app/src/test/java/com/noop/food/FoodVisionRequestTest.kt
@@ -39,8 +39,7 @@ class FoodVisionRequestTest {
         assertTrue(text.getString("text").contains("Spanish"))
 
         val outputConfig = body.getJSONObject("output_config")
-        assertEquals(setOf("format", "effort"), outputConfig.keySet())
-        assertEquals("high", outputConfig.getString("effort"))
+        assertEquals(setOf("format"), outputConfig.keySet())
         val format = outputConfig.getJSONObject("format")
         assertEquals("json_schema", format.getString("type"))
         assertEquals(FoodVision.outputSchema().toString(), format.getJSONObject("schema").toString())
@@ -55,10 +54,10 @@ class FoodVisionRequestTest {
         assertTrue(at.all { it >= 0 })
         assertEquals(at, at.sorted())
         assertTrue(prompt.contains("partly hidden"))                      // hidden layers under other food
-        assertTrue(prompt.contains("never from a typical serving"))       // no regression to a standard serving
         assertTrue(prompt.contains("26 cm") && prompt.contains("19 cm"))  // plate and cutlery as size references
-        assertTrue(prompt.contains("most often underestimated"))          // the published bias
-        assertTrue(prompt.contains("olive oil") && prompt.contains("as its own item")) // cooking fat listed, visible, editable
+        assertTrue(prompt.contains("visual cue") && prompt.contains("olive oil") && prompt.contains("as its own item")) // fat on evidence, visible, editable
+        // No push in either direction: a nudge against under-estimation made the model over-estimate weighed plates.
+        assertFalse(prompt.contains("underestimated") || prompt.contains("typical serving") || prompt.contains("about 10 g"))
         assertTrue(prompt.contains("PER 100 g") && prompt.contains("grams × per 100 g"))
         assertTrue(prompt.contains("the photo cannot show"))              // the correction the wearer can make
         assertTrue(prompt.contains("from Spain"))
@@ -70,7 +69,7 @@ class FoodVisionRequestTest {
             val body = FoodVision.buildRequestBody("m", listOf("x"), "", structured)
             for (k in banned) assertFalse("$k must not be sent", body.has(k))
             assertFalse(body.toString().contains("\"temperature\""))
-            assertFalse("effort lives inside output_config", body.has("effort"))
+            assertFalse("no effort setting: the default sized portions as well as high at half the cost", body.toString().contains("\"effort\""))
         }
     }
 
